course: dictionary
lesson: 3772
title: Folly: silliness or a strange building
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Folly» can mean silliness, or an act or idea that is very unwise. Look for clues in the sentence: «It would be folly to walk home alone in the dark.» The words unwise and dark tell you that the choice is foolish.
explain: The same word can also name a strange building. Some were built in big parks or gardens just for show, and they look like a tower or a fake ruin. In «the folly on the hill», there is no silly act at all. The hill and the tower are the clues.
explain: Always test your meaning in the sentence. Swap in «silliness» for folly: «The Badger saw Toad's silliness with the motor cars.» It still makes sense, so silliness is the right meaning in that story.
fact: Folly means foolishness, or a very silly or unwise act or idea.
fact: «The folly of greed» means the foolishness of wanting too much, and stories often use it as a lesson.
fact: A folly can also be a strange decorative building in a big park or garden, built just for show, like a fake ruin or a tower.
fact: On country walks in Britain and Ireland you may see a folly tower on a hill.
fact: Useful phrases: «sheer folly», «the height of folly», and «it would be folly to…».
exercise: «It would be folly to go out in that storm.» What does folly mean here? | *Silliness, a very unwise choice | A show with dancing and songs | A tall tower on a hill | Being sorry for something
exercise: In The Wind in the Willows, the Badger and Rat try to save Toad from his folly with motor cars. What does folly mean? | *Silly, unwise behaviour | Speed on the open road | Friendship and kindness | Riding a horse
exercise: Walking on the hill, you see a tall stone tower that was built just for show. What is it most likely to be? | A lighthouse for ships | A railway station | *A folly
test:
«And it wasn't folly at all!» In the story, what does this mean? | *It was not silly or unwise | It was a tall tower on a hill | It was a dance show with songs | It was very sad news
«The height of folly» means what? | Being very tall | Being very happy | *The most foolish thing you can do | Being sorry for something you did
exam: Which sentence uses folly to mean a building? | The folly of greed taught them a lesson | It would be folly to climb that wall in the rain | Her folly was to spend all her money in one day | *The stone folly on the hill was built just for show
